hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24231","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah, narrating from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended Sa'd ibn Ubadah. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I find a man on my wife's belly, shall I strike him with my sword? He said: What proof is clearer than the sword? He said: Then he retracted his saying and said: The Book of Allah and the witnesses. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, what proof is clearer than the sword? He said: The Book of Allah and the witnesses. O company of Ansar, this chief of yours, jealousy has provoked him until he opposed the Book of Allah. He said: So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, Sa'd is jealous, and he has never divorced a wife but that none of us could marry her due to his jealousy. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sa'd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah is more jealous than me. A man said: For what does Allah feel jealousy? He said: For a man striving in the path of Allah who goes to his family unfaithfully."
"24232","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ya'qub ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah, who said: Among our houses there was a weak, sick, premature little man. The neighborhood noticed nothing but that he was with one of their slave girls, committing indecency with her. He said: So Sa'd ibn Ubadah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that little man was a Muslim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strike him his prescribed punishment. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, he is weaker than that; if we struck him a hundred, we would kill him. So he said: Take for him a palm-branch cluster containing a hundred stalks, then strike him with it one strike. He said: So they did."
